1
00:00:00,825 --> 00:00:02,204
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:02,224 --> 00:00:03,274
A caterpillar!

3
00:00:03,574 --> 00:00:05,804
One day, it will become a butterfly.

4
00:00:06,084 --> 00:00:09,174
Is the caterpillar a nymph, like the young grasshopper?

5
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:10,330
One, yes.

6
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:12,430
Two, no.

7
00:00:13,908 --> 00:00:15,418
Hold on to your answer!

8
00:00:17,290 --> 00:00:19,620
A little moth is hiding in this video.

9
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:21,110
Can you spot it?

10
00:00:21,234 --> 00:00:22,884
Moths rest in the daytime.

11
00:00:22,984 --> 00:00:24,974
Look on the walls, and under the leaves!

12
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:26,484
You against the Buddies!

13
00:00:26,754 --> 00:00:28,604
Lock in first with your fingers.

14
00:00:28,874 --> 00:00:30,704
One finger for every point.

15
00:00:31,285 --> 00:00:32,615
Today you'll learn:

16
00:00:32,811 --> 00:00:34,691
The 4-stage life cycle.

17
00:00:34,890 --> 00:00:36,400
Larva and pupa.

18
00:00:36,652 --> 00:00:37,870
What prolegs are.

19
00:00:38,464 --> 00:00:39,404
Are you ready?

20
00:00:39,844 --> 00:00:40,614
Three!

21
00:00:40,994 --> 00:00:41,654
Two!

22
00:00:42,024 --> 00:00:42,674
One!

23
00:00:43,094 --> 00:00:43,814
Go!

24
00:00:45,203 --> 00:00:46,093
Round one!

25
00:00:46,403 --> 00:00:48,033
Is the caterpillar a nymph?

26
00:00:48,323 --> 00:00:49,633
Show me your fingers!

27
00:00:53,101 --> 00:00:54,081
Locked in!

28
00:00:54,209 --> 00:00:58,549
One! It is a young insect that munches leaves, just like the grasshopper

29
00:00:58,569 --> 00:00:59,209
nymph.

30
00:00:59,449 --> 00:01:00,799
So it must be a nymph!

31
00:01:00,846 --> 00:01:04,036
Two. A nymph looks like a small adult.

32
00:01:04,236 --> 00:01:07,346
But this caterpillar looks nothing like a butterfly.

33
00:01:07,448 --> 00:01:09,544
Two! A butterfly has big wings.

34
00:01:09,564 --> 00:01:13,376
This caterpillar is just a long, green tube that eats!

35
00:01:13,685 --> 00:01:16,315
The answer is two: no, it is not a nymph!

36
00:01:16,595 --> 00:01:17,625
Two fingers?

37
00:01:17,895 --> 00:01:19,105
One finger up!

38
00:01:19,232 --> 00:01:20,532
Then what is it?

39
00:01:20,552 --> 00:01:22,722
It is long and soft, and it wriggles.

40
00:01:22,762 --> 00:01:23,962
Is it a worm?

41
00:01:24,611 --> 00:01:25,761
Look closer.

42
00:01:26,351 --> 00:01:28,081
Count the legs at the front.

43
00:01:28,651 --> 00:01:30,704
Then look at the little stumps at the back.

44
00:01:30,724 --> 00:01:33,844
One, two, three pairs of pointed legs at the front.

45
00:01:33,934 --> 00:01:36,456
That is six legs, so it is an insect!

46
00:01:36,476 --> 00:01:39,656
Like all insects, caterpillars have six legs.

47
00:01:40,243 --> 00:01:43,003
The stumps at the back are not real legs.

48
00:01:43,573 --> 00:01:45,333
They are called prolegs.

49
00:01:46,393 --> 00:01:48,783
Prolegs are pretend legs with tiny hooks.

50
00:01:48,803 --> 00:01:51,573
The hooks grip the twig, so the caterpillar can hold on and

51
00:01:51,593 --> 00:01:52,683
crawl along!

52
00:01:55,388 --> 00:01:56,538
Say it with me!

53
00:01:57,252 --> 00:02:00,512
Prolegs are false legs that help the caterpillars to move.

54
00:02:03,285 --> 00:02:04,675
Be a butterfly egg!

55
00:02:04,985 --> 00:02:05,975
Shrink down.

56
00:02:06,255 --> 00:02:07,185
Quietly.

57
00:02:09,472 --> 00:02:12,492
You are a tiny round egg, stuck on a lime leaf.

58
00:02:13,272 --> 00:02:15,282
Days go by, and you hatch.

59
00:02:16,062 --> 00:02:17,712
You are a little caterpillar!

60
00:02:18,223 --> 00:02:20,563
You munch the leaf, and munch, and munch.

61
00:02:21,343 --> 00:02:24,703
Your skin gets tight, so you moult, and you grow bigger.

62
00:02:25,217 --> 00:02:26,987
One day, you stop eating.

63
00:02:27,787 --> 00:02:29,647
You hang very still from a stem.

64
00:02:30,166 --> 00:02:32,346
Your skin splits one last time.

65
00:02:33,146 --> 00:02:35,236
Underneath, there is a hard case.

66
00:02:36,026 --> 00:02:37,256
You are a pupa!

67
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:42,400
The butterfly larva is also called a caterpillar.

68
00:02:42,911 --> 00:02:45,541
So the caterpillar is the butterfly's larva.

69
00:02:45,661 --> 00:02:49,031
A larva is the young, and it looks nothing like the adult!

70
00:02:49,082 --> 00:02:52,752
The larva eats a lot and moults many times as it grows.

71
00:02:53,488 --> 00:02:55,988
Now it does not move, and it does not eat.

72
00:02:56,138 --> 00:02:57,858
So nothing is happening in there.

73
00:02:57,878 --> 00:02:59,998
It is just resting!

74
00:03:00,127 --> 00:03:01,687
Something is not right.

75
00:03:01,957 --> 00:03:04,137
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

76
00:03:04,417 --> 00:03:05,377
Hold on!

77
00:03:10,790 --> 00:03:11,920
Arms crossed?

78
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:13,400
One finger up!

79
00:03:13,452 --> 00:03:16,032
It does not eat, but it is alive and very busy.

80
00:03:16,272 --> 00:03:19,322
Inside its case, it is changing into a butterfly!

81
00:03:19,452 --> 00:03:21,492
This stage is called the pupa.

82
00:03:23,582 --> 00:03:24,732
Look closer.

83
00:03:25,362 --> 00:03:28,142
On the outside, the pupa hardly moves.

84
00:03:28,692 --> 00:03:31,982
But inside the pupal case, the body is changing.

85
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:33,350
It does not eat.

86
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:37,710
It continues to develop into an adult in the pupal case.

87
00:03:38,222 --> 00:03:41,152
So the pupa is busy, like a cake in the oven.

88
00:03:41,262 --> 00:03:44,522
You cannot see it change, but it is changing inside!

89
00:03:45,703 --> 00:03:50,113
Then the pupal case splits, and out comes the adult: a butterfly!

90
00:03:51,023 --> 00:03:54,413
Its wings are all crumpled, like my bedsheet in the morning.

91
00:03:54,653 --> 00:03:56,323
Now they are spreading out flat!

92
00:03:59,303 --> 00:04:02,473
The butterfly has four stages in its life cycle.

93
00:04:02,733 --> 00:04:06,603
The stages are the egg, the larva, the pupa and the adult.

94
00:04:08,217 --> 00:04:09,507
Say it with me!

95
00:04:10,213 --> 00:04:13,343
Some animals have four stages in their life cycles.

96
00:04:13,823 --> 00:04:16,873
The young of these animals do not look like the adult.

97
00:04:19,349 --> 00:04:20,819
Show me your score hand!

98
00:04:21,089 --> 00:04:22,409
More than one finger?

99
00:04:22,729 --> 00:04:24,089
You beat the Buddies.

100
00:04:24,369 --> 00:04:25,399
Two fingers?

101
00:04:25,669 --> 00:04:26,679
High five!

102
00:04:27,257 --> 00:04:28,707
Did you spot the moth?

103
00:04:28,957 --> 00:04:31,347
It was on the side of the lime plant's pot!

104
00:04:31,484 --> 00:04:33,074
Here is a fun fact!

105
00:04:33,254 --> 00:04:37,254
Many moth caterpillars spin a silk cocoon, and become a pupa inside

106
00:04:37,274 --> 00:04:40,994
it. The silk for silk clothes comes from a moth's cocoon!

107
00:04:41,116 --> 00:04:42,396
Tell someone at home!

108
00:04:43,125 --> 00:04:45,325
Let's read today's key words together!

109
00:04:45,615 --> 00:04:46,375
Ready?

110
00:04:46,712 --> 00:04:47,465
Prolegs.

111
00:04:48,997 --> 00:04:49,657
Larva.

112
00:04:51,157 --> 00:04:51,957
Pupa.

113
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:54,274
Well done!

114
00:04:55,071 --> 00:04:57,001
Look in this old pail of rainwater!

115
00:04:57,181 --> 00:04:59,131
Tiny things are wriggling up and down.

116
00:04:59,341 --> 00:05:00,262
What are they?

117
00:05:00,282 --> 00:05:01,872
Find out in Part Two!

118
00:05:03,032 --> 00:05:04,133
Say it with us!

119
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:05,683
Ready?

120
00:05:05,807 --> 00:05:06,467
One!

121
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:07,507
two!

122
00:05:07,812 --> 00:05:08,987
Now you know!
